{"title": "Sectional Mock #11 (Mixed)", "duration_min": 30.0, "questions": [{"q_en": "<p>There are total 568 students in a school. If number of girls in school are two-third more than the number of boys in the school. How many girls are there in the school?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2367;&#2342;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2354;&#2351; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2325;&#2369;&#2354; 568 &#2331;&#2366;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2357;&#2367;&#2342;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2354;&#2351; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2354;&#2337;&#2364;&#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;, &#2354;&#2337;&#2364;&#2325;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2360;&#2375; 2/3 &#2309;&#2343;&#2367;&#2325; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2357;&#2367;&#2342;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2354;&#2351; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2354;&#2337;&#2364;&#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["325", "335", "345", "355"], "options_hi": ["325", "335", "345", "355"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>Total number of students = 568</p><p>Let number of boys = n</p><p>Then, number of girls = (1 + 2/3) * n = 5n/3</p><p>Now, 568 = n + 5n/3</p><p>n = 213</p><p>Therefore, number of girls = 568  -  213 = <b>355</b></p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Total number of students = 568</p><p>Let number of boys = n</p><p>Then, number of girls = (1 + 2/3) * n = 5n/3</p><p>Now, 568 = n + 5n/3</p><p>n = 213</p><p>Therefore, number of girls = 568  -  213 = <b>355</b></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Number System"}, {"q_en": "<p>If a<sup>2</sup> + b<sup>2</sup> = 84 and ab = 30, and a, b&gt;0. Find the value of (a<sup>3</sup> + b<sup>3</sup>).</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; a<sup>2</sup> + b<sup>2</sup> = 84 &#2324;&#2352; ab = 30 &#2340;&#2341;&#2366; a, b&gt;0 &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; (a<sup>3</sup> + b<sup>3</sup>) &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["745", "564", "648", "450"], "options_hi": ["745", "564", "648", "450"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>a<sup>2</sup> + b<sup>2</sup> = 84 and ab = 30</p><p>(a + b)<sup>2</sup> = a<sup>2</sup> + b<sup>2</sup> + 2ab</p><p>(a + b)<sup>2</sup> = 84 + 2*30 = 84 + 60 = 144</p><p>a + b = 12</p><p>(a + b)<sup>3</sup> = a<sup>3</sup> + b<sup>3</sup> + 3ab(a + b)</p><p>a<sup>3</sup> + b<sup>3</sup> = 12<sup>3</sup>  -  3*30*12</p><p>= 12(144-90)</p><p>= 12*54</p><p>= 648</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>a<sup>2</sup> + b<sup>2</sup> = 84 and ab = 30</p><p>(a + b)<sup>2</sup> = a<sup>2</sup> + b<sup>2</sup> + 2ab</p><p>(a + b)<sup>2</sup> = 84 + 2*30 = 84 + 60 = 144</p><p>a + b = 12</p><p>(a + b)<sup>3</sup> = a<sup>3</sup> + b<sup>3</sup> + 3ab(a + b)</p><p>a<sup>3</sup> + b<sup>3</sup> = 12<sup>3</sup>  -  3*30*12</p><p>= 12(144-90)</p><p>= 12*54</p><p>= 648</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Algebra"}, {"q_en": "<p>At a gaming arcade, all game tokens cost the same, and there is an additional entry fee of &#8377;200. Virat played 10 games and spent a total of &#8377;1,000 during his visit. How much (in &#8377;) would Virat have to pay if he played 16 games?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2327;&#2375;&#2350;&#2367;&#2306;&#2327; &#2310;&#2352;&#2381;&#2325;&#2375;&#2337; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;, &#2360;&#2349;&#2368; &#2327;&#2375;&#2350; &#2335;&#2379;&#2325;&#2344; &#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2368;&#2350;&#2340; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2324;&#2352; &#2357;&#2361;&#2366;&#2306; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2357;&#2375;&#2358; &#2358;&#2369;&#2354;&#2381;&#2325; &#2325;&#2375; &#2352;&#2370;&#2346; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 200 &#2337;&#2377;&#2354;&#2352; &#2309;&#2340;&#2367;&#2352;&#2367;&#2325;&#2381;&#2340; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2357;&#2367;&#2352;&#2366;&#2335; &#2344;&#2375; 10 &#2327;&#2375;&#2350; &#2326;&#2375;&#2354;&#2375; &#2324;&#2352; &#2309;&#2346;&#2344;&#2368; &#2351;&#2366;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2375; &#2342;&#2380;&#2352;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2369;&#2354; 1,000 &#2337;&#2377;&#2354;&#2352; &#2326;&#2352;&#2381;&#2330; &#2325;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404; &#2309;&#2327;&#2352; &#2357;&#2367;&#2352;&#2366;&#2335; &#2344;&#2375; 16 &#2327;&#2375;&#2350; &#2326;&#2375;&#2354;&#2375; &#2340;&#2379; &#2313;&#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; (1,000 &#2337;&#2377;&#2354;&#2352; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;) &#2349;&#2369;&#2327;&#2340;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2379;&#2327;&#2366;?</p>", "options_en": ["Rs.1620", "Rs.1290", "Rs.1380", "Rs.1480"], "options_hi": ["&#2352;&#2369;.1620", "&#2352;&#2369;.1290", "&#2352;&#2369;.1380", "&#2352;&#2369;.1480"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>Let the cost of one token be Rs. X</p><p>Given that,</p><p>10 games + entry fee = Rs.1000</p><p>10X + 200 = 1000</p><p>10X = 800</p><p>X = 80</p><p>If the number of games is 16, then total amount paid by Virat = 16 X 80 + 200 = 1280 + 200 = Rs.1480</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let the cost of one token be Rs. X</p><p>Given that,</p><p>10 games + entry fee = Rs.1000</p><p>10X + 200 = 1000</p><p>10X = 800</p><p>X = 80</p><p>If the number of games is 16, then total amount paid by Virat = 16 X 80 + 200 = 1280 + 200 = Rs.1480</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Ratio & Proportion"}, {"q_en": "<p>In what ratio must a grocer mix two varieties of pulses costing &#8377;15 and &#8377;20 per kg, respectively, so as to get a mixture worth &#8377;18 per kg?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2346;&#2306;&#2360;&#2366;&#2352;&#2368; &#2325;&#2379; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;&#2307; &#8377;15 &#2324;&#2352; &#8377;20 &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367; kg &#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2368;&#2350;&#2340; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2368; &#2342;&#2379; &#2325;&#2367;&#2360;&#2381;&#2350; &#2325;&#2368; &#2342;&#2366;&#2354;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2379; &#2325;&#2367;&#2360; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2350;&#2367;&#2354;&#2366;&#2344;&#2366; &#2330;&#2366;&#2361;&#2367;&#2319;, &#2332;&#2367;&#2360;&#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2367; &#8377;18 &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367; kg &#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2368;&#2350;&#2340; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2366; &#2319;&#2325; &#2350;&#2367;&#2358;&#2381;&#2352;&#2339; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2346;&#2381;&#2340; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366; &#2360;&#2325;&#2375;?</p>", "options_en": ["3:5", "3:4", "2:3", "2:5"], "options_hi": ["3:5", "3:4", "2:3", "2:5"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Let the ratio in which two varieties are mixed = x: 1</p><p>According to the question:</p><p>x * 15 + 1 * 20 = (x + 1) * 18</p><p>15x + 20 = 18x + 18</p><p>3x = 2</p><p>x = 2/3</p><p>Hence, required ratio = 2: 3</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let the ratio in which two varieties are mixed = x: 1</p><p>According to the question:</p><p>x * 15 + 1 * 20 = (x + 1) * 18</p><p>15x + 20 = 18x + 18</p><p>3x = 2</p><p>x = 2/3</p><p>Hence, required ratio = 2: 3</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mixture & Alligation"}, {"q_en": "<p>A person started running around a circular track of radius 21 meters with speed of 39.6 km/h. Find the time taken to finish one complete round of the track.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2325;&#2381;&#2340;&#2367; &#2344;&#2375; 21 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2375; &#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2366;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2335;&#2381;&#2352;&#2376;&#2325; &#2325;&#2375; &#2311;&#2352;&#2381;&#2342;-&#2327;&#2367;&#2352;&#2381;&#2342; 39.6 km/h &#2325;&#2368; &#2330;&#2366;&#2354; &#2360;&#2375; &#2342;&#2380;&#2337;&#2364;&#2344;&#2366; &#2310;&#2352;&#2306;&#2349; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366;&#2404; &#2335;&#2381;&#2352;&#2376;&#2325; &#2325;&#2366; &#2319;&#2325; &#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2366; &#2330;&#2325;&#2381;&#2325;&#2352; &#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2354;&#2327;&#2344;&#2375; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2366; &#2360;&#2350;&#2351; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["8 sec", "16 sec", "10 sec", "12 sec"], "options_hi": ["8 &#2360;&#2375;&#2325;&#2306;&#2337;", "16 &#2360;&#2375;&#2325;&#2306;&#2337;", "10 &#2360;&#2375;&#2325;&#2306;&#2337;", "12 &#2360;&#2375;&#2325;&#2306;&#2337;"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>Total running length = 2&#960;r = 2 * (22/7) * 21</p><p>Speed = 39.6 km/h = 39.6 * (5/18) = 11 m/sec</p><p>Time taken to finish one complete round of the track = 2 * (22/7) * 21 &div; 11</p><p>= 12 sec</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Total running length = 2&#960;r = 2 * (22/7) * 21</p><p>Speed = 39.6 km/h = 39.6 * (5/18) = 11 m/sec</p><p>Time taken to finish one complete round of the track = 2 * (22/7) * 21 &div; 11</p><p>= 12 sec</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mensuration (2D)"}, {"q_en": "<p>Two pipes P and Q fill a tank in 140 minutes and 52.5 minutes respectively. A third pipe R can empty it at __ liters/minute. When all three pipes are opened together, then the tank is filled in 1 hour. If the capacity of the tank is 630 liters, then what should come in place of the given blank?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2342;&#2379; &#2346;&#2366;&#2311;&#2346; P &#2324;&#2352; Q &#2319;&#2325; &#2335;&#2376;&#2306;&#2325; &#2325;&#2379; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;&#2307; 140 &#2350;&#2367;&#2344;&#2335; &#2324;&#2352; 52.5 &#2350;&#2367;&#2344;&#2335; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2349;&#2352;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; &#2319;&#2325; &#2340;&#2368;&#2360;&#2352;&#2366; &#2346;&#2366;&#2311;&#2346; R &#2311;&#2360;&#2375; __&#2354;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352;/&#2350;&#2367;&#2344;&#2335; &#2325;&#2368; &#2342;&#2352; &#2360;&#2375; &#2326;&#2366;&#2354;&#2368; &#2325;&#2352; &#2360;&#2325;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2332;&#2348; &#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2366;&#2341; &#2340;&#2368;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2346;&#2366;&#2311;&#2346;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2379; &#2326;&#2379;&#2354; &#2342;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2335;&#2306;&#2325;&#2368; 1 &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2349;&#2352; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2335;&#2376;&#2306;&#2325; &#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2350;&#2340;&#2366; 630 &#2354;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2342;&#2367;&#2319; &#2327;&#2319; &#2352;&#2367;&#2325;&#2381;&#2340; &#2360;&#2381;&#2341;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2375; &#2360;&#2381;&#2341;&#2366;&#2344; &#2346;&#2352; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2310;&#2344;&#2366; &#2330;&#2366;&#2361;&#2367;&#2319;?</p>", "options_en": ["8", "4", "6", "9"], "options_hi": ["8", "4", "6", "9"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>P = 140 minutes, Q = 52.5 minutes</p><p>When all pipes are opened together, then the tank is filled in 1 hour (or 60 minutes). This means filling rate is more than the emptying rate. So,</p><p>1/60 = 1/P + 1/Q  -  1/R</p><p>1/60 = 1/140 + 1/52.5  -  1/R</p><p>R = 105 minutes</p><p>Let R can empty the tank it at X liters/minute.</p><p>Since, the capacity of the tank is 630 liters, then</p><p>X = 630/105</p><p><b>X = 6</b></p>", "solution_hi": "<p>P = 140 minutes, Q = 52.5 minutes</p><p>When all pipes are opened together, then the tank is filled in 1 hour (or 60 minutes). This means filling rate is more than the emptying rate. So,</p><p>1/60 = 1/P + 1/Q  -  1/R</p><p>1/60 = 1/140 + 1/52.5  -  1/R</p><p>R = 105 minutes</p><p>Let R can empty the tank it at X liters/minute.</p><p>Since, the capacity of the tank is 630 liters, then</p><p>X = 630/105</p><p><b>X = 6</b></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Pipes & Cisterns"}, {"q_en": "<p>Sam completed a work in 36 days and Veer is 80% more efficient than Sam. They start working together, but Veer left the work after 9 days due to some issue, then Sam alone can complete the remaining work in:</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2360;&#2376;&#2350; &#2319;&#2325; &#2325;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2351; &#2325;&#2379; 36 &#2342;&#2367;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; &#2340;&#2341;&#2366; &#2357;&#2368;&#2352;, &#2360;&#2376;&#2350; &#2360;&#2375; 80% &#2309;&#2343;&#2367;&#2325; &#2325;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2351; &#2325;&#2369;&#2358;&#2354; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2357;&#2375; &#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2366;&#2341; &#2325;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2351; &#2358;&#2369;&#2352;&#2370; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;, &#2354;&#2375;&#2325;&#2367;&#2344; &#2357;&#2368;&#2352; 9 &#2342;&#2367;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2366;&#2342; &#2325;&#2367;&#2360;&#2368; &#2360;&#2350;&#2360;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2375; &#2325;&#2366;&#2352;&#2339; &#2325;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2351; &#2331;&#2379;&#2337;&#2364; &#2342;&#2375;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2360;&#2376;&#2350; &#2309;&#2325;&#2375;&#2354;&#2375; &#2358;&#2375;&#2359; &#2325;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2351; &#2325;&#2379; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2375; &#2342;&#2367;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2352; &#2360;&#2325;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["9.6 days", "11.2 days", "10.8 days", "10.2 days"], "options_hi": ["9.6 &#2342;&#2367;&#2344;", "11.2 &#2342;&#2367;&#2344;", "10.8 &#2342;&#2367;&#2344;", "10.2 &#2342;&#2367;&#2344;"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Sam alone completed the work in 36 days.</p><p>Thus, Veer alone completed the work in = 36 * 100/180 = 20 days</p><p>In 9 days, part of work done by Sam and Veer = 9 * (1/36 + 1/20) = 7/10</p><p>So, remaining work = 1  -  7/10 = 3/10</p><p>Hence, Sam alone can complete the remaining work in = 3/10 * 36 = 10.8 days</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Sam alone completed the work in 36 days.</p><p>Thus, Veer alone completed the work in = 36 * 100/180 = 20 days</p><p>In 9 days, part of work done by Sam and Veer = 9 * (1/36 + 1/20) = 7/10</p><p>So, remaining work = 1  -  7/10 = 3/10</p><p>Hence, Sam alone can complete the remaining work in = 3/10 * 36 = 10.8 days</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Time & Work"}, {"q_en": "<p>If LCM and HCF of two numbers are 819 and 13 respectively and one number is 91, then what is the other number?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2342;&#2379; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366; LCM &#2324;&#2352; HCF &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;&#2307; 819 &#2324;&#2352; 13 &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; 91 &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2342;&#2370;&#2360;&#2352;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["104", "117", "143", "156"], "options_hi": ["104", "117", "143", "156"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>One number * another number = LCM * HCF</p><p>=&gt; 91 * another number = 819 * 13</p><p>=&gt; another number = 819 * 13/91</p><p>=&gt; another number = 117</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>One number * another number = LCM * HCF</p><p>=&gt; 91 * another number = 819 * 13</p><p>=&gt; another number = 819 * 13/91</p><p>=&gt; another number = 117</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "HCF & LCM"}, {"q_en": "<p>How many different words of 10 letters are possible using the letters of the word TELEVISION if it contains two I's together?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>TELEVISION &#2358;&#2348;&#2381;&#2342; &#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2352;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366; &#2313;&#2346;&#2351;&#2379;&#2327; &#2325;&#2352;&#2325;&#2375; 10 &#2309;&#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2352;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2375; &#2309;&#2354;&#2327;-&#2309;&#2354;&#2327; &#2358;&#2348;&#2381;&#2342; &#2360;&#2306;&#2349;&#2357; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;, &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2311;&#2360;&#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2342;&#2379; I &#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2366;&#2341; &#2361;&#2379;&#2306;?</p>", "options_en": ["36*7!", "5*9!", "18*7!", "4*7!"], "options_hi": ["36*7!", "5*9!", "18*7!", "4*7!"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>In the word TELEVISION, there are 10 letters =&gt; 2I (which are together so count as one place), 2E are repeated.</p><p>Total number of ways = 9!/2! = 36*7!</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>In the word TELEVISION, there are 10 letters =&gt; 2I (which are together so count as one place), 2E are repeated.</p><p>Total number of ways = 9!/2! = 36*7!</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mixed Practice"}, {"q_en": "<p>Golu and Sona started a business investing Rs.18300 and Rs.21000 respectively. In what ratio the profit earned after 2 years be divided between Golu and Sona respectively?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2327;&#2379;&#2354;&#2370; &#2324;&#2352; &#2360;&#2379;&#2344;&#2366; &#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;&#2307; 18300 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2324;&#2352; 21000 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2325;&#2366; &#2344;&#2367;&#2357;&#2375;&#2358; &#2325;&#2352;&#2325;&#2375; &#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2357;&#2360;&#2366;&#2351; &#2358;&#2369;&#2352;&#2370; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366;&#2404; 2 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359; &#2348;&#2366;&#2342; &#2309;&#2352;&#2381;&#2332;&#2367;&#2340; &#2354;&#2366;&#2349; &#2325;&#2379; &#2327;&#2379;&#2354;&#2370; &#2324;&#2352; &#2360;&#2379;&#2344;&#2366; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2368;&#2330; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;&#2307; &#2325;&#2367;&#2360; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2357;&#2367;&#2349;&#2366;&#2332;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2319;&#2327;&#2366;?</p>", "options_en": ["53: 60", "63: 85", "61: 70", "71: 83"], "options_hi": ["53: 60", "63: 85", "61: 70", "71: 83"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Profit ratio after 2 years = 18300 * 2: 21000 * 2</p><p>= 61: 70</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Profit ratio after 2 years = 18300 * 2: 21000 * 2</p><p>= 61: 70</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Profit & Loss"}, {"q_en": "<p>Shivangi has lent some money to Shivani at 21.5% p.a. and Shweta at 28% p.a. At the end of the year, he has gained an overall interest at the rate of 24%. In what ratio has he lent the money to Shivani and Shweta?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2358;&#2367;&#2357;&#2366;&#2306;&#2327;&#2368; &#2344;&#2375; &#2358;&#2367;&#2357;&#2366;&#2344;&#2368; &#2325;&#2379; 21.5% &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359; &#2324;&#2352; &#2358;&#2381;&#2357;&#2375;&#2340;&#2366; &#2325;&#2379; 28% &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359; &#2325;&#2368; &#2342;&#2352; &#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2369;&#2331; &#2346;&#2376;&#2360;&#2375; &#2313;&#2343;&#2366;&#2352; &#2342;&#2367;&#2319; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359; &#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2306;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;, &#2313;&#2360;&#2375; 24% &#2325;&#2368; &#2342;&#2352; &#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2369;&#2354; &#2348;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2332; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2346;&#2381;&#2340; &#2361;&#2369;&#2310; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2313;&#2360;&#2344;&#2375; &#2358;&#2367;&#2357;&#2366;&#2344;&#2368; &#2324;&#2352; &#2358;&#2381;&#2357;&#2375;&#2340;&#2366; &#2325;&#2379; &#2325;&#2367;&#2360; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2346;&#2376;&#2360;&#2375; &#2313;&#2343;&#2366;&#2352; &#2342;&#2367;&#2319; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;?</p>", "options_en": ["5: 3", "9: 7", "8: 5", "7: 4"], "options_hi": ["5: 3", "9: 7", "8: 5", "7: 4"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p><img width=298 height=105 id=\"Picture 5\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p27152/image005.png\"></p><p>4% 2.5%</p><p>8 5</p><p>Hence, the required ratio is 8: 5.</p>", "solution_hi": "<p><img width=298 height=105 id=\"Picture 5\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p27152/image005.png\"></p><p>4% 2.5%</p><p>8 5</p><p>Hence, the required ratio is 8: 5.</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mixture & Alligation"}, {"q_en": "<p>The average weight of 3 men A, B and C is 84 kg. Another man D joins the group and the average now becomes 80 kg. If another man E, whose weight is 3 kg more than that of D, replaces A then the average weight of B, C, D and E becomes 78 kg. The weight of A is ___.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2340;&#2368;&#2344; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2325;&#2381;&#2340;&#2367;&#2351;&#2379;&#2306; A,B &#2324;&#2352; C &#2325;&#2366; &#2324;&#2360;&#2340; &#2349;&#2366;&#2352; 84 &#2325;&#2367;&#2354;&#2379;&#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2350; &#2361;&#2376;| &#2319;&#2325; &#2309;&#2344;&#2381;&#2351; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2325;&#2381;&#2340;&#2367; &#2360;&#2350;&#2370;&#2361; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2358;&#2366;&#2350;&#2367;&#2354; &#2361;&#2379;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2309;&#2348; &#2324;&#2360;&#2340; 80 &#2325;&#2367;&#2354;&#2379;&#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2350; &#2361;&#2379; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;| &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2319;&#2325; &#2324;&#2352; &#2309;&#2344;&#2381;&#2351; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2325;&#2381;&#2340;&#2367; E &#2332;&#2367;&#2360;&#2325;&#2366; &#2349;&#2366;&#2352; D &#2325;&#2375; &#2349;&#2366;&#2352; &#2360;&#2375; 3 &#2325;&#2367;&#2354;&#2379;&#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2350; &#2309;&#2343;&#2367;&#2325; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2357;&#2361; A &#2325;&#2375; &#2360;&#2381;&#2341;&#2366;&#2344; &#2346;&#2352; &#2310; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; &#2332;&#2367;&#2360;&#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2367; B, C, D &#2324;&#2352; E &#2325;&#2366; &#2324;&#2360;&#2340; &#2349;&#2366;&#2352; 78 &#2325;&#2367;&#2354;&#2379;&#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2350; &#2361;&#2379; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;| A &#2325;&#2366; &#2349;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["70 kg", "72 kg", "79 kg", "78 kg"], "options_hi": ["70 &#2325;&#2367;&#2354;&#2379;&#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2350;", "72 &#2325;&#2367;&#2354;&#2379;&#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2350;", "79 &#2325;&#2367;&#2354;&#2379;&#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2350;", "78 &#2325;&#2367;&#2354;&#2379;&#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2350;"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Sum of weights of A, B and C = 3 X 84 = 252 kg</p><p>Sum of weights of A, B, C and D = 4 X 80 = 320 kg</p><p>Weight of D = 320  -  252 = 68 kg</p><p> Weight of E = 68 + 3 = 71 kg</p><p>Now, sum of weights of A, B, C, D and E = 320 + 71</p><p>Sum of weights of B, C, D and E = 4 X 78 = 312 kg</p><p> Weight of A = 391  -  312 = 79 kg.</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Sum of weights of A, B and C = 3 X 84 = 252 kg</p><p>Sum of weights of A, B, C and D = 4 X 80 = 320 kg</p><p>Weight of D = 320  -  252 = 68 kg</p><p> Weight of E = 68 + 3 = 71 kg</p><p>Now, sum of weights of A, B, C, D and E = 320 + 71</p><p>Sum of weights of B, C, D and E = 4 X 78 = 312 kg</p><p> Weight of A = 391  -  312 = 79 kg.</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Average"}, {"q_en": "<p>If A and B are events with P(A) = 4/15, P(B) = 1/20, and P(A' &#1352; B') = 7/10. Fins P(A &#1352; B).</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; A &#2324;&#2352; B &#2328;&#2335;&#2344;&#2366;&#2319;&#2305; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306; &#2332;&#2367;&#2344;&#2350;&#2375;&#2306; P(A) = 4/15, P(B) = 1/20, &#2340;&#2341;&#2366; P(A' &#1352; B') = 7/10 &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; P(A &#1352; B) &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2346;&#2381;&#2340; &#2325;&#2352;&#2375;&#2306;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["1/30", "3/20", "1/12", "1/60"], "options_hi": ["1/30", "3/20", "1/12", "1/60"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>P (A' &#1352; B') = 1  -  [P(A) + P(B)  -  P (A &#1352; B)]</p><p>7/10 = 1  -  [4/15 + 1/20  -  P (A &#1352; B)]</p><p>4/15 + 1/20  -  P (A &#1352; B) = 3/10 </p><p>P (A &#1352; B) = (16 + 3  -  18)/60 </p><p>P (A &#1352; B) = 1/60 </p>", "solution_hi": "<p>P (A' &#1352; B') = 1  -  [P(A) + P(B)  -  P (A &#1352; B)]</p><p>7/10 = 1  -  [4/15 + 1/20  -  P (A &#1352; B)]</p><p>4/15 + 1/20  -  P (A &#1352; B) = 3/10 </p><p>P (A &#1352; B) = (16 + 3  -  18)/60 </p><p>P (A &#1352; B) = 1/60 </p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Probability"}, {"q_en": "<p>Rashmi deposited Rs.40000 in a bank which is giving compound interest at the rate of 20% per annum. What will be her interest in the 3<sup>rd</sup> year?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2352;&#2358;&#2381;&#2350;&#2368; &#2344;&#2375; &#2319;&#2325; &#2348;&#2376;&#2306;&#2325; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2352;&#2369;. 40000 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2332;&#2350;&#2366; &#2325;&#2367;&#2319; &#2332;&#2379; 20% &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359; &#2325;&#2368; &#2342;&#2352; &#2360;&#2375; &#2330;&#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2357;&#2371;&#2342;&#2381;&#2343;&#2367; &#2348;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2332; &#2342;&#2375; &#2352;&#2361;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2340;&#2368;&#2360;&#2352;&#2375; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2313;&#2360;&#2325;&#2366; &#2348;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2332; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2379;&#2327;&#2366;?</p>", "options_en": ["Rs.11520", "Rs.9820", "Rs.10120", "Rs.12320"], "options_hi": ["&#2352;&#2369;.11520", "&#2352;&#2369;.9820", "&#2352;&#2369;.10120", "&#2352;&#2369;.12320"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>Interest in the 3<sup>rd</sup> year = Amount received after 3 years  -  Amount received after 2 years</p><p><img width=247 height=49 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p24278/image001.png\"></p><p><img width=137 height=29 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p24278/image002.png\"></p><p><img width=105 height=19 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p24278/image003.png\"></p><p><img width=77 height=19 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p24278/image004.png\"></p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Interest in the 3<sup>rd</sup> year = Amount received after 3 years  -  Amount received after 2 years</p><p><img width=247 height=49 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p24278/image001.png\"></p><p><img width=137 height=29 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p24278/image002.png\"></p><p><img width=105 height=19 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p24278/image003.png\"></p><p><img width=77 height=19 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p24278/image004.png\"></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Simple & Compound Interest"}, {"q_en": "<p>Which part contains the fractions in ascending order?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2325;&#2380;&#2344; &#2360;&#2366; &#2349;&#2366;&#2327; &#2349;&#2367;&#2344;&#2381;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2379; &#2310;&#2352;&#2379;&#2361;&#2368; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2352;&#2326;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["20/27 &lt; 16/21 &lt; 18/23 &lt; 21/25", "21/25 &lt; 18/23 &lt; 20/27 &lt; 16/21", "16/21 &lt; 18/23 &lt; 20/27 &lt; 21/25", "18/23 &lt; 20/27 &lt; 21/25 &lt; 16/21"], "options_hi": ["20/27 &lt; 16/21 &lt; 18/23 &lt; 21/25", "21/25 &lt; 18/23 &lt; 20/27 &lt; 16/21", "16/21 &lt; 18/23 &lt; 20/27 &lt; 21/25", "18/23 &lt; 20/27 &lt; 21/25 &lt; 16/21"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>21/25 = 0.84, 18/23 = 0.78, 16/21 = 0.76, 20/27= 0.74</p><p>Hence, ascending order = 20/27 &lt; 16/21 &lt; 18/23 &lt; 21/25</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>21/25 = 0.84, 18/23 = 0.78, 16/21 = 0.76, 20/27= 0.74</p><p>Hence, ascending order = 20/27 &lt; 16/21 &lt; 18/23 &lt; 21/25</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Number System"}, {"q_en": "<p>What is the length of intercepts of line 12x  -  28y + 21 = 0 between two axes?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2342;&#2379; &#2309;&#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2368;&#2330; &#2352;&#2375;&#2326;&#2366; 12x - 28y + 21 = 0 &#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2306;&#2340;&#2307;&#2326;&#2306;&#2337;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2366;&#2312; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["&radic;52/4 unit", "&radic;54/4 unit", "&radic;56/4 unit", "&radic;58/4 unit"], "options_hi": ["&radic;52/4 &#2311;&#2325;&#2366;&#2312;", "&radic;54/4 &#2311;&#2325;&#2366;&#2312;", "&radic;56/4 &#2311;&#2325;&#2366;&#2312;", "&radic;58/4 &#2311;&#2325;&#2366;&#2312;"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>12x  -  28y + 21 = 0</p><p>12x  -  28y = -21</p><p>(12x/-21)  -  (28y/-21) = 1</p><p>(4x/-7) + (4y/3) = 1</p><p>[x/(-7/4)] + [y/(3/4)] = 1</p><p>Intercept of line of the form (x/a) + (y/b) = 1 at x and y axes is 'a' and 'b' respectively.</p><p>Length of intercept = &radic;(a<sup>2</sup> + b<sup>2</sup>)</p><p>Intercept of given line at x and y axes is '-7/4' and '3/4' respectively.</p><p>Length of intercept = &radic;[(-7/4)<sup>2</sup> + (3/4)<sup>2</sup>] = &radic;58/4 unit</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>12x  -  28y + 21 = 0</p><p>12x  -  28y = -21</p><p>(12x/-21)  -  (28y/-21) = 1</p><p>(4x/-7) + (4y/3) = 1</p><p>[x/(-7/4)] + [y/(3/4)] = 1</p><p>Intercept of line of the form (x/a) + (y/b) = 1 at x and y axes is 'a' and 'b' respectively.</p><p>Length of intercept = &radic;(a<sup>2</sup> + b<sup>2</sup>)</p><p>Intercept of given line at x and y axes is '-7/4' and '3/4' respectively.</p><p>Length of intercept = &radic;[(-7/4)<sup>2</sup> + (3/4)<sup>2</sup>] = &radic;58/4 unit</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Algebra"}, {"q_en": "<p>A shopkeeper sells some quantity of oats at the cost price, but he uses false weight of 'X' gm instead of 1000 gm and gain 5% profit. Find the quantity of oats he gives instead of 1000 g. (rounded off to two decimals)</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2342;&#2369;&#2325;&#2366;&#2344;&#2342;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2369;&#2331; &#2350;&#2366;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2323;&#2335;&#2381;&#2360; &#2325;&#2379; &#2354;&#2366;&#2327;&#2340; &#2350;&#2370;&#2354;&#2381;&#2351; &#2346;&#2352; &#2348;&#2375;&#2330;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2354;&#2375;&#2325;&#2367;&#2344; &#2357;&#2361; 1000 &#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2350; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2332;&#2366;&#2351; 'X' &#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2350; &#2325;&#2366; &#2327;&#2354;&#2340; &#2357;&#2332;&#2344; &#2311;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2375;&#2350;&#2366;&#2354; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; 5% &#2354;&#2366;&#2349; &#2325;&#2350;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; 1000 &#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2350; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2332;&#2366;&#2351; &#2357;&#2361; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2368; &#2350;&#2366;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2323;&#2335;&#2381;&#2360; &#2342;&#2375;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2351;&#2361; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404; (&#2342;&#2379; &#2342;&#2358;&#2350;&#2354;&#2357; &#2340;&#2325; &#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2381;&#2339;&#2366;&#2306;&#2325;&#2367;&#2340;)</p>", "options_en": ["962.86 gm", "978.17 gm", "943.45 gm", "952.38 gm"], "options_hi": ["962.86 &#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2350;", "978.17 &#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2350;", "943.45 &#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2350;", "952.38 &#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2350;"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>Quantity of oats given instead of 1000 gm = X gm</p><p>Profit percentage = 5%</p><p>X = [1000/(100 + 5)] * 100</p><p>X = 952.38 gm</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Quantity of oats given instead of 1000 gm = X gm</p><p>Profit percentage = 5%</p><p>X = [1000/(100 + 5)] * 100</p><p>X = 952.38 gm</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Profit & Loss"}, {"q_en": "<p>On a field, there is a vertical pillar with a tower on its top. At a point 14 meters away from the foot of the pillar, the angles of elevation of the top and bottom of the tower are 60&#176; and 45&#176; respectively. Find the difference of the height of the pillar and the tower.</p><p></p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2350;&#2376;&#2342;&#2366;&#2344; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;, &#2319;&#2325; &#2314;&#2352;&#2381;&#2343;&#2381;&#2357;&#2366;&#2343;&#2352; &#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2306;&#2349; &#2361;&#2376; &#2332;&#2367;&#2360;&#2325;&#2375; &#2358;&#2368;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359; &#2346;&#2352; &#2319;&#2325; &#2335;&#2366;&#2357;&#2352; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2306;&#2349; &#2325;&#2375; &#2346;&#2366;&#2342; &#2360;&#2375; 14 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2325;&#2368; &#2342;&#2370;&#2352;&#2368; &#2346;&#2352;, &#2335;&#2366;&#2357;&#2352; &#2325;&#2375; &#2314;&#2346;&#2352; &#2324;&#2352; &#2344;&#2368;&#2330;&#2375; &#2325;&#2375; &#2313;&#2344;&#2381;&#2344;&#2351;&#2344; &#2325;&#2379;&#2339; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;&#2307; 60&deg; &#2324;&#2352; 45&deg; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; &#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2306;&#2349; &#2324;&#2352; &#2335;&#2366;&#2357;&#2352; &#2325;&#2368; &#2314;&#2305;&#2330;&#2366;&#2312; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2306;&#2340;&#2352; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["14&#8730;3 - 28 meters", "14 &#8211; 11/&#8730;3 meters", "28 &#8211; 11/&#8730;3 meters", "28 &#8211; 14&#8730;3 meters"], "options_hi": ["14&radic;3 - 28 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352;", "14 - 11/&radic;3 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352;", "28 - 11/&radic;3 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352;", "28 - 14/&radic;3 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352;"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "\"<p>Calculation:</p><p><img src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/stubeimg/7783878.png\"><br></p><p>In a triangle BCD,</p><p> &#8658; tan 45&#176; = BD/BC</p><p> &#8658; 1 = BD/14</p><p> &#8658; BD = 14 meters (Pillar)</p><p>In a triangle ABC,</p><p> &#8658; tan 60&#176; = AB/BC</p><p> &#8658; &#8730;3 = AB/14</p><p> &#8658; AB = 14&#8730;3 (Pillar + Tower)</p><p> &#8658; AD = AB &#8211; BD = (14&#8730;3)- 14</p><p> &#8658; AD = 14(&#8730;3 - 1)</p><p> &#8658; The difference of the height of the pillar and the tower = BD - AD</p><p> &#8658; 14 - 14(&#8730;3 - 1)</p><p> &#8658; 28 - 14&#8730;3</p><p></p>\"", "solution_hi": "\"<p>Calculation:</p><p><img src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/stubeimg/7783878.png\"><br></p><p>In a triangle BCD,</p><p> &#8658; tan 45&#176; = BD/BC</p><p> &#8658; 1 = BD/14</p><p> &#8658; BD = 14 meters (Pillar)</p><p>In a triangle ABC,</p><p> &#8658; tan 60&#176; = AB/BC</p><p> &#8658; &#8730;3 = AB/14</p><p> &#8658; AB = 14&#8730;3 (Pillar + Tower)</p><p> &#8658; AD = AB &#8211; BD = (14&#8730;3)- 14</p><p> &#8658; AD = 14(&#8730;3 - 1)</p><p> &#8658; The difference of the height of the pillar and the tower = BD - AD</p><p> &#8658; 14 - 14(&#8730;3 - 1)</p><p> &#8658; 28 - 14&#8730;3</p><p></p>\"", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Height & Distance"}, {"q_en": "<p>If tan&#952; = 3/5, then find the value of (1 + sec&#952;)(1  -  sec&#952;)/(1 + cosec&#952;)(1  -  cosec&#952;).</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; tan&#952; = 3/5, &#2340;&#2379; (1 + sec&#952;)(1 - sec&#952;)/(1 + cosec&#952;)(1 - cosec&#952;) &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["9/25", "25/9", "81/625", "625/81"], "options_hi": ["9/25", "25/9", "81/625", "625/81"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>tan&#952; = 3/5</p><p>(1 + sec&#952;)(1  -  sec&#952;)/(1 + cosec&#952;)(1  -  cosec&#952;)</p><p>= (sec<sup>2</sup>&#952;  -  1)/(cosec<sup>2</sup>&#952;  -  1)</p><p>= tan<sup>2</sup>&#952;/cot<sup>2</sup>&#952;</p><p>= tan<sup>4</sup>&#952;</p><p>= (3/5)<sup>4</sup></p><p>= 81/625</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>tan&#952; = 3/5</p><p>(1 + sec&#952;)(1  -  sec&#952;)/(1 + cosec&#952;)(1  -  cosec&#952;)</p><p>= (sec<sup>2</sup>&#952;  -  1)/(cosec<sup>2</sup>&#952;  -  1)</p><p>= tan<sup>2</sup>&#952;/cot<sup>2</sup>&#952;</p><p>= tan<sup>4</sup>&#952;</p><p>= (3/5)<sup>4</sup></p><p>= 81/625</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Trigonometry"}, {"q_en": "<p>15 men or 20 women can do a piece of work in 24 days. Find the time taken by 10 men and 8 women working together to do the double of that work.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>15 &#2346;&#2369;&#2352;&#2369;&#2359; &#2351;&#2366; 20 &#2350;&#2361;&#2367;&#2354;&#2366;&#2319;&#2305; &#2325;&#2367;&#2360;&#2368; &#2325;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2351; &#2325;&#2379; 24 &#2342;&#2367;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2325;&#2352; &#2360;&#2325;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; &#2313;&#2360; &#2325;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2351; &#2325;&#2366; &#2342;&#2379;&#2327;&#2369;&#2344;&#2366; &#2349;&#2366;&#2327; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2366;&#2341; 10 &#2346;&#2369;&#2352;&#2369;&#2359;&#2379;&#2306; &#2324;&#2352; 8 &#2350;&#2361;&#2367;&#2354;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2342;&#2381;&#2357;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2354;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2327;&#2351;&#2366; &#2360;&#2350;&#2351; &#2360;&#2350;&#2351; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2351;&#2375;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["30 days", "15 days", "45 days", "60 days"], "options_hi": ["30 &#2342;&#2367;&#2344;", "15 &#2342;&#2367;&#2344;", "45 &#2342;&#2367;&#2344;", "60 &#2342;&#2367;&#2344;"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Let the time taken by 10 men and 8 women together is 'T'.</p><p>15M = 20W</p><p>3M = 4W</p><p>The total worker = 10 men + 8 women = 10 men + 8 women = 16 men</p><p>15M * 24/1 = 16M * T/2 </p><p>T = 15 M * 24 * 2/16 = 45 days</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let the time taken by 10 men and 8 women together is 'T'.</p><p>15M = 20W</p><p>3M = 4W</p><p>The total worker = 10 men + 8 women = 10 men + 8 women = 16 men</p><p>15M * 24/1 = 16M * T/2 </p><p>T = 15 M * 24 * 2/16 = 45 days</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Time & Work"}, {"q_en": "<p>A man can row at 45kmph in still water, and he finds that it takes him four times as much time to row upstream as to row downstream for the same distance in the river. Find the speed of the stream.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2310;&#2342;&#2350;&#2368; &#2360;&#2381;&#2341;&#2367;&#2352; &#2346;&#2366;&#2344;&#2368; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 45 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367; &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375; &#2325;&#2368; &#2342;&#2352; &#2360;&#2375; &#2344;&#2366;&#2357; &#2330;&#2354;&#2366; &#2360;&#2325;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2357;&#2361; &#2346;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; &#2325;&#2367; &#2344;&#2342;&#2368; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2342;&#2370;&#2352;&#2368; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; &#2343;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2325;&#2370;&#2354; &#2344;&#2366;&#2357; &#2330;&#2354;&#2366;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2368; &#2340;&#2369;&#2354;&#2344;&#2366; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2343;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2375; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2325;&#2370;&#2354; &#2344;&#2366;&#2357; &#2330;&#2354;&#2366;&#2344;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2313;&#2360;&#2375; &#2330;&#2366;&#2352; &#2327;&#2369;&#2344;&#2366; &#2309;&#2343;&#2367;&#2325; &#2360;&#2350;&#2351; &#2354;&#2327;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2344;&#2342;&#2368; &#2325;&#2368; &#2343;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2368; &#2327;&#2340;&#2367; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["32kmph", "18kmph", "22kmph", "27kmph"], "options_hi": ["32 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2366;", "18 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2366;", "22 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2366;", "27 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2366;"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>Let the speed of the stream be X</p><p>Then, 45 + x = 4(45-x)</p><p>45 + x = 180  -  4x</p><p>5x = 135</p><p>X = 27kmph</p><p>Hence, speed of the stream = 27kmph</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let the speed of the stream be X</p><p>Then, 45 + x = 4(45-x)</p><p>45 + x = 180  -  4x</p><p>5x = 135</p><p>X = 27kmph</p><p>Hence, speed of the stream = 27kmph</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Time, Speed & Distance"}, {"q_en": "<p>From the table given below, find the percentage of employees whose income is less than Rs.25000.</p><table style=\"border-collapse:collapse;\"><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">Income (in thousand)</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">5 to 10</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">10 to 15</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">15 to 20</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">20 to 25</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">25 to 30</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">30 to 35</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">35 to 40</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">Number of employees</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">7</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">16</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">23</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">9</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">42</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">43</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">25</td></tr></table>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2344;&#2368;&#2330;&#2375; &#2342;&#2368; &#2327;&#2312; &#2340;&#2366;&#2354;&#2367;&#2325;&#2366; &#2360;&#2375;, &#2313;&#2344; &#2325;&#2352;&#2381;&#2350;&#2330;&#2366;&#2352;&#2367;&#2351;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2358;&#2340; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2352;&#2375;&#2306;, &#2332;&#2367;&#2344;&#2325;&#2368; &#2310;&#2351; 25000 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2350; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404;</p><table style=\"border-collapse:collapse;\"><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">&#2310;&#2351; (&#2361;&#2332;&#2366;&#2352; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;)</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">5 &#2360;&#2375; 10</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">10 &#2360;&#2375; 15</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">15 &#2360;&#2375; 20</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">20 &#2360;&#2375; 25</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">25 &#2360;&#2375; 30</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">30 &#2360;&#2375; 35</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">35 &#2360;&#2375; 40</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">&#2325;&#2352;&#2381;&#2350;&#2330;&#2366;&#2352;&#2367;&#2351;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">7</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">16</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">23</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">9</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">42</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">43</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">25</td></tr></table>", "options_en": ["33.33%", "66.67%", "50%", "47.5%"], "options_hi": ["33.33%", "66.67%", "50%", "47.5%"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>Total number of employees = 7 + 16 + 23 + 9 + 42 + 43 + 25 = 165</p><p>Number of employees whose income is less than Rs.25000 = 7 + 16 + 23 + 9 = 55</p><p>Therefore, percentage = (55/165) * 100 = <b>33.33%</b></p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Total number of employees = 7 + 16 + 23 + 9 + 42 + 43 + 25 = 165</p><p>Number of employees whose income is less than Rs.25000 = 7 + 16 + 23 + 9 = 55</p><p>Therefore, percentage = (55/165) * 100 = <b>33.33%</b></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Percentage"}, {"q_en": "<p>In a rectangular field, the sum of the length and the breadth is 9 cm and area is 18 cm<sup>2</sup>. If the length is 'a' and breadth is 'b', then find the value of (a<sup>2</sup> &#8722; ab + b<sup>2</sup>).</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2310;&#2351;&#2340;&#2366;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2350;&#2376;&#2342;&#2366;&#2344; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;, &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2366;&#2312; &#2324;&#2352; &#2330;&#2380;&#2337;&#2364;&#2366;&#2312; &#2325;&#2366; &#2351;&#2379;&#2327; 9 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; 18 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;<sup>2</sup>&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2366;&#2312; 'a' &#2324;&#2352; &#2330;&#2380;&#2337;&#2364;&#2366;&#2312; 'b' &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; (a<sup>2</sup> &#8722; ab + b<sup>2</sup>) &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["36", "24", "18", "27"], "options_hi": ["36", "24", "18", "27"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>Sum of length and breadth:</p><p>a + b = 9</p><p>Area of the rectangle:</p><p>a  X  b = 18</p><p>We can rewrite a<sup>2</sup>  -  ab + b<sup>2</sup> as (a + b)<sup>2</sup>  -  3ab</p><p>Now, substitute these values into the equation:</p><p>=&gt; a&#178; - ab + b&#178; = (9)&#178; - 3  X  18</p><p>=&gt; 81  -  54 = 27</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Sum of length and breadth:</p><p>a + b = 9</p><p>Area of the rectangle:</p><p>a  X  b = 18</p><p>We can rewrite a<sup>2</sup>  -  ab + b<sup>2</sup> as (a + b)<sup>2</sup>  -  3ab</p><p>Now, substitute these values into the equation:</p><p>=&gt; a&#178; - ab + b&#178; = (9)&#178; - 3  X  18</p><p>=&gt; 81  -  54 = 27</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mensuration (2D)"}, {"q_en": "<p>The minimum value of some observation is 379 and range is 71, then what is the maximum value?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2325;&#2367;&#2360;&#2368; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2375;&#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2339; &#2325;&#2366; &#2344;&#2381;&#2351;&#2370;&#2344;&#2340;&#2350; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; 379 &#2340;&#2341;&#2366; &#2346;&#2352;&#2367;&#2360;&#2352; 71 &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2309;&#2343;&#2367;&#2325;&#2340;&#2350; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2379;&#2327;&#2366;?</p>", "options_en": ["420", "450", "430", "530"], "options_hi": ["420", "450", "430", "530"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>We know that,</p><p>Max value  -  min value = Range</p><p>Max value = 71 + 379 = 450</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>We know that,</p><p>Max value  -  min value = Range</p><p>Max value = 71 + 379 = 450</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Statistics"}, {"q_en": "<p>A cylindrical cup of diameter 4cm and height 4cm is used to fill a hemispherical bowl of radius 6cm. How many cups will be required to fill the hemispherical bowl</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2360; 4cm &#2324;&#2352; &#2314;&#2306;&#2330;&#2366;&#2312; 4cm &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; &#2319;&#2325; &#2348;&#2375;&#2354;&#2344;&#2366;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2346; &#2325;&#2366; &#2313;&#2346;&#2351;&#2379;&#2327; 6cm &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; &#2309;&#2352;&#2381;&#2343;&#2327;&#2379;&#2354;&#2368;&#2351; &#2325;&#2335;&#2379;&#2352;&#2375; &#2325;&#2379; &#2349;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2309;&#2352;&#2381;&#2343;&#2327;&#2379;&#2354;&#2366;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2335;&#2379;&#2352;&#2375; &#2325;&#2379; &#2349;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2346;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2310;&#2357;&#2358;&#2381;&#2351;&#2325;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2379;&#2327;&#2368;?</p>", "options_en": ["12", "10", "7", "9"], "options_hi": ["12", "10", "7", "9"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>Volume of a cup = &#960;r<sup>2</sup>H = &#960;  X  (4/2)<sup>2</sup>  X  4 = 16&#960; cm<sup>3</sup></p><p>Volume of bowl = <img width=172 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p21411/image009.png\"></p><p>Number of cups required to fill the bowl = 144&#960;/16&#960; = 9</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Volume of a cup = &#960;r<sup>2</sup>H = &#960;  X  (4/2)<sup>2</sup>  X  4 = 16&#960; cm<sup>3</sup></p><p>Volume of bowl = <img width=172 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p21411/image009.png\"></p><p>Number of cups required to fill the bowl = 144&#960;/16&#960; = 9</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mensuration (3D)"}]}